      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can see this working as\n\n- a separate launch option (vrchat.exe --offline) meant for testing purposes but which could be used for any cached world as you said\n\n- a custom instance mode (which would disable world-related network sync BUT not prevent receiving invites, as you can already do that through status modes)\n\n- an optional mode when loosing connection to an instance (eg: prompt allowing one to stay in-world when loosing internet)\n\nHowever tbh, if other players are the main concern, using invite-only instances while being on red should be enough for now. The fact that worlds require an internet connection to load anyway (and that the game has a very forgiving sync system, with high ping being quite playable still) might make such system a bit useless. Still, I like the idea.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
