      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An offline mode could also be very useful for people who want to use VRChat for media production, or even for streaming, reducing the network overhead and negating any interruptions due to connection issues with VRChat.\n\nI see it working similar to how you can launch your own worlds in offline test mode from Unity.\n\nIt being a specific launch option, and requiring some prep work, like say, tagging specific content (worlds, avatars) to be cached for offline mode would be OK, no need to add anything to the base UI.\n\nPersonally, appart from media production, I also love spending time alone on certain worlds lost in my own thoughts. Being able to just put the headset on and launch into my preferred world without having to worry about an internet connection would be great. I mean, it would certainly be a corner case, but using VRChat offline in this manner when say, on a long train or plane trip, would be really neat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-03-30T18:27:56.149Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Unstable internet connection but still want to sleep in a world, test avis/worlds without interference or play clientside game worlds? (Such as Idle Home, a commonly played \"singleplayer\" experience) How about an option to run worlds and avatars you already have cached (or can cache in online mode) so that you can stay on? This could also be an option to have as default for home worlds, saving server space from individual users logging in. There may also be drawbacks, ranging from video players not functioning (depending on how the system works), and being unable to invite others (it may show you as offline as well), but for those on the platform who are introverted, this is a potential option to have an experience to yourself with no disruptions.",
